# Drafted by Gemini (R11 batch b1), edited. doris_squire's first conversation.

~ start
set doris_squire_met
Narrator: Iron keys clink against her belt, and the smell of cold tallow and scrubbed stone hangs round her like a cloak.
doris_squire [neutral]: Strangers. Keep your blades sheathed in the Round and we will get on fine.
* Ask about the law in Wickermoor -> about_work
* Ask about the village -> about_village
* Ask about the law and the jail -> shop_open
* Ask about the oak in the square -> rumour
* [Perception DC 14] Glance at the small paper tucked under her blotter -> secret_ok | secret_fail
* Take our leave -> END

~ about_work
doris_squire [neutral]: Three barred cells behind me, fines for brawling, banishment for grand theft. Spill blood in murder and the Mayor takes your head before the Oak of Many Faces.
-> menu

~ about_village
doris_squire [weary]: Good folk mostly, when they are not spooked by moor-fog or preaching at each other in the mud. Do your business before the late bells and stay on the lantern paths.
-> menu

~ shop_open
doris_squire [neutral]: If you want honest coin, there is the bounty board.
-> menu

~ rumour
doris_squire [neutral]: Every face in that bark was a name on the parish roll once. The roots drink deep after a sentence, and the moss stays red for a week.
-> menu

~ secret_ok
Narrator: Beneath a brass sunflower weight lies a scrap of foolscap written in neat verse about rain on quiet wheat.
doris_squire [angry]: Eyes on my face, traveler, not on my desk. A woman is allowed a bit of quiet ink between lockups.
-> menu

~ secret_fail
Narrator: Her broad hand covers the blotter like a slate slab dropping into place.
doris_squire [neutral]: Charge sheets are for the watch, not for tourists.
-> menu

~ menu
* Ask about the law in Wickermoor -> about_work
* Ask about the village -> about_village
* Ask about the law and the jail -> shop_open
* Ask about the oak in the square -> rumour
* [Perception DC 14] Glance at the small paper tucked under her blotter -> secret_ok | secret_fail
* Take our leave -> END
